# Testing

> Applies to Plexo's unit, integration, browser, sidecar, load, and regression checks.

## Test inventory

- `pnpm test:all` runs Turborepo package tests plus `tests/unit` and `tests/integration`.
- `pnpm test:e2e` runs the Playwright suite under `tests/e2e/`; live-stack setup uses `pnpm e2e:up` and teardown uses `pnpm e2e:down`.
- TypeScript package tests are colocated under `src/` or under the package's test directory; repository-wide unit and integration tests live under `tests/unit/` and `tests/integration/`.
- Browser tests live under `tests/e2e/`; load and chaos checks live under `tests/load/` and `tests/chaos/`.
- API route source is primarily `apps/api/src/routes/`; Next.js route handlers also live under `apps/web/src/app/api/`.

## Testability

- Pure rules and use cases should run without a database, server, network, or framework boot.
- Test adapters at the boundary they call. Prefer injected fakes where a port exists; mock auth at the route boundary for route tests.
- When query count or order changes, inspect every sequential mock in the affected tests; passing assertions can still read the wrong result.
- Never skip, `.only`, comment out, or delete a failing test to get green.

## Endpoint coverage target

Every endpoint should have behavior coverage in the same change. Plexo has no route-test coverage checker or allowlist, and this setup does not scaffold one because the required tooling files are outside the configuration-only scope. Review must enforce the pairing until that machinery is separately approved and wired.

- For `apps/api/src/routes/`, use the nearest route test, `apps/api/src/routes/__tests__/`, `apps/api/src/__tests__/`, or an applicable integration/e2e suite according to the existing area convention.
- For `apps/web/src/app/api/`, keep tests beside the route or in the nearest existing web test area.
- Cover success status and exact response shape, validation failures, authz/not-found paths, and accepted pagination/filtering.
- Do not add an allowlist entry to hide a missing test.

## Mocking

- Mock authentication/authorization at the route boundary so endpoint tests focus on endpoint behavior.
- Inject fakes through ports rather than patching internals. Mock at the boundary the code actually calls.
- If no port exists in legacy code, record the missing boundary rather than hiding it with deeper mocks.

## Required validation

- Full unit/integration/package run: `pnpm test:all`.
- Browser validation when UI or endpoint wiring changes: `pnpm test:e2e`.
- Full typecheck: `pnpm typecheck`.
- Lint: `pnpm lint`.
- Array-bind gate: `pnpm check:sql-arrays`. Interpolating a JS array into a `sql` template does not
  bind an array — Drizzle expands it to a row constructor, so `ANY(${ids}::uuid[])` fails at runtime
  and typechecks clean. Use `sqlArray(values, type)` from `packages/agent/src/sql-array.ts`.
- Architecture boundaries: `pnpm arch:check`. It reads `.dependency-cruiser-baseline.json`, a ratchet
  of known violations — delete the entries your change fixes, and never regenerate the baseline.
